<LegalLayout
  title="Shipping Policy"
  description="Shipping, delivery, customs, and risk information for products purchased through authorized resellers."
>
  <h2>1. We do not ship products</h2>
  <p>
    Davis Weather Station is an independent directory and does not sell or ship products. Shipping is arranged and
    fulfilled by the authorized reseller you choose. This page explains what to expect and what to confirm with the
    reseller.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Reseller fulfilment</h2>
  <p>
    Each reseller sets its own delivery areas, carriers, processing times, shipping rates, and delivery options.
    Some resellers ship internationally; others only serve their own country or region. Confirm coverage and lead
    times before ordering.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Delivery times</h2>
  <p>
    Delivery estimates are provided by the reseller and are not guarantees. Weather, customs, carrier delays, public
    holidays, remote locations, and stock availability can affect delivery. Made-to-order or configured systems may
    take longer.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Shipping costs</h2>
  <p>
    Shipping charges are set by the reseller and may depend on destination, weight, dimensions, insurance, and
    speed. Any free-shipping offer is the reseller’s promotion and may have conditions.
  </p>

  <h2>5. International orders, customs, and taxes</h2>
  <p>
    For cross-border orders, import duties, taxes, brokerage fees, and customs clearance charges may apply. These
    are usually the buyer’s responsibility unless the reseller states otherwise. The reseller and carrier can explain
    what to expect for your destination.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Risk of loss and title</h2>
  <p>
    Risk of loss and transfer of title are governed by the reseller’s terms and applicable law. If a parcel is lost
    or damaged in transit, contact the reseller and the carrier promptly so they can investigate and process a claim.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Tracking</h2>
  <p>
    Where tracking is available, the reseller or carrier will provide a tracking number. Tracking updates can lag
    behind actual movement, especially for international shipments.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Address accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    Provide a complete and accurate delivery address, including unit, building, postal code, and contact number.
    The reseller may not be able to redirect a parcel after dispatch, and address-correction fees may apply.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Shipping questions should go to the reseller you ordered from. You can find their contact details in our{' '}
    <a href="/resellers/">reseller directory</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
